## Support scripts — the `SupportScripts` repo

The Python tooling for this project lives in a **separate repo**,
`SupportScripts` (sibling directory `../SupportScripts`). See its `README.md` and
`CLAUDE.md` for full documentation. In brief:

| Script | Job |
|---|---|
| `tracker_to_csv.py` | Google Sheet (`Daily Log`) → `cleanups/cleanups.csv` for **Tools → Import Cleanups CSV**. `.xlsx` fallback. Config in `config.toml` + `credentials.json` (both now in `SupportScripts`). Point it back here with `-o ../glc/cleanups/cleanups.csv`. |
| `monthly_infographic.py` | Monthly impact infographic for Instagram — HTML template screenshotted with headless Chromium. Reads the **raw** tracker CSV (needs the separate `Cans (#)` / `Bottles (#)` columns; the merged `cleanups/cleanups.csv` is rejected). Assets + output live next to the script. |
| `prepare_wildlife_asset.py` | Background removal + crop for `/stats/` wildlife card images and `_s.png` map-pin crops. (Was `remove_background.py`.) |
| `prepare_corridors_geojson.py` | Offline fetch of river/creek line geometry (OSM) → `plugin-dev/great-lake-cleaners/assets/corridors.geojson`. |
| `site_audit.py` | Read-only security/health audit of production; `--post` exercises the public forms for real. Run after every deploy. The invariants it guards are documented in `CLAUDE.md`. |
| `resize_uploads.py` | Batch-downscale images in a directory, in place. |

**tracker_to_csv.py merge behaviour:** same date + same location → one event,
numeric fields summed; same date + different location → separate events. Volunteer
hours = Σ person-hours. Instagram URL and GPS = first non-empty. Duplicate
date+site pairs are skipped by the importer.

## Outing Tracker

**Primary source:** Google Sheet (native format only — not xlsx stored in Drive)  
**Local backup:** `Great_Lake_Cleaners_Outing_Tracker.xlsx`  
**Tab name:** `Daily Log`

### Column Layout (0-based)

| Index | Excel col | Field | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | A | Date | |
| 1 | B | Location / Corridor | Must match exactly for same-site merging |
| 2 | C | Duration (min) | |
| 3 | D | Bags (#) | Garbage |
| 4 | E | Weight (kg) | Garbage |
| 5 | F | Notes | Imported into post_content |
| 6 | G | Cans (#) | Recycling |
| 7 | H | Bottles (#) | Recycling |
| 8 | I | Recyclables Weight (kg) | Weight of cans + bottles — tracked separately, not added to debris weight |
| 9 | J | Number of people | Volunteers |
| 10 | K | Notable / Unusual Finds | |
| 11 | L | Latitude | GPS — enter on first visit to a new site |
| 12 | M | Longitude | GPS — negative for Ontario |
| 13 | N | Instagram Post URL | Link to field log |
| 14 | O | Corridor | Matches known corridor names for badge display |
| 15 | P | Tires (#) | Car/truck tires only — feeds [glc_impact_highlights] tire total. Bicycle tires used to be counted here; split out to Bikes 2026-08 |
| 16 | Q | Bikes (#) | Count of whole bicycles removed — feeds [glc_impact_highlights] bike total. New column added 2026-08; add it to the Google Sheet after column P |

**Volunteer hours** = duration × volunteers. 70 min × 2 people = 2.33h.
**GPS:** enter once per new location. Blank = no map pin.
**Date format:** Script normalises to `YYYY-MM-DD`. Store as date values in Google Sheets, not text.

The `COL_*` index constants at the top of `tracker_to_csv.py` and
`monthly_infographic.py` (in `SupportScripts`) mirror this table — update all
three together if the Sheet grows a column.

